      "seconds_since_start": 0.076,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.076
    },
    "text": "I can look into this \u2014 Lake Formation cross-account sharing issues usually come down to one of a few things: the RAM share not being accepted in the consumer account, missing LF-Tag or named-resource permissions granted to the consumer, the consumer's Glue catalog not having the resource link created, or an IAM/LF settings mismatch (e.g., consumer account not enabling the \"Grantable\" permission or using the wrong catalog ID).\n\nTo check this properly, I need a few specifics:\n\n1. **The producer account ID** that owns and shared the database (is this the agent space account, 012345678901_1, or a different one?)\n2. **The consumer account ID** that can't see the share\n3. **The Glue database name** being shared\n4. **The AWS region**\n\nOnce I have those, I'll check the Lake Formation permissions, the RAM resource share status, and the catalog settings on both sides."
  },
